<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Thirty-first Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">343 BCE – 332 BCE · capital Memphis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Egypt's brief second period of Persian rule, from Artaxerxes III's reconquest to the arrival of Alexander the Great.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After failed attempts in 351 BCE, the Persian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-iii">Artaxerxes III</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 343 BCE, defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nectanebo-ii">Nectanebo II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thirtieth-dynasty-of-egypt">Thirtieth Dynasty of Egypt</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pelusium">Pelusium</a> and capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/memphis-egypt">Memphis</a>. Egypt again became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manetho">Manetho</a> counts the Persian kings as the Thirty-first Dynasty.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Greek writers describe a harsh reconquest, with temple treasures looted and city walls destroyed, though some stories, such as the killing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apis">Apis bull</a>, may be propaganda. A local rebel, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khababash">Khababash</a>, briefly held power in the Delta in the late 330s BCE. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrapy</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/memphis-egypt">Memphis</a>, had to face unrest while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> itself suffered the murders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-iii">Artaxerxes III</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artaxerxes-iv">Arses</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-issus">Issus</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazaces">Mazaces</a> surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> without a fight in 332 BCE, and it passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a> and later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ptolemaic-empire">Ptolemaic Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/thirty-first-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Thirty-first Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="324"><figcaption>Image: Mossmaps · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_part_of_the_Achaemenid_Empire.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>343 BCE – 332 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Memphis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Artaxerxes III, Arses, Darius III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion, Zoroastrianism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian, Aramaic, Old Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Second Persian Period, Thirty-first Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-338&amp;focus=thirty-first-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Thirty-first Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5493 1088 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Thirty-first Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5813 1344L6140 1251M5813 1344L5808 1305M5813 1344L5548 987"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6140 1251h0M5808 1305h0M5548 987h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5813 1344h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5813 1344h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Memphis. <a href="/atlas?year=-338&amp;focus=thirty-first-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
